{{Main|Without You (Mariah Carey recording)}}
American singer and songwriter [[Mariah Carey]]'s version, based on Harry Nilsson's version rather than the Badfinger original, was released as the third single off ''[[Music Box (Mariah Carey album)|Music Box]]'' in the first quarter of 1994. Its US release date of 21 January 1994 by [[Columbia Records]] fell a week after Nilsson's death following a heart attack on 15 January 1994. In the US "Without You" was promoted as a double A-side with "[[Never Forget You (Mariah Carey song)|Never Forget You]]". While she had heard Nilsson's version as a very young girl, Carey's decision to remake his hit was based on a chance hearing during the recording of ''Music Box'': "I heard that song in a restaurant and just knew it would be a huge international hit" recalls Carey.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-news/american-idol-recap-candice-glover-steals-the-show-again-67454/|title=Candice Steals the Show on 'American Idol'|first=Melissa|last=Locker|website=Rolling Stone|date=18 April 2013|access-date=24 April 2021|archive-date=25 January 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210125082324/https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-news/american-idol-recap-candice-glover-steals-the-show-again-67454/|url-status=live}}</ref> Carey's version has been considered very popular on talent shows.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.mcarchives.com/news/spec.asp?id=6098|archive-url=https://archive.today/20120910180519/http://www.mcarchives.com/news/spec.asp?id=6098|url-status=dead|archive-date=10 September 2012|title=Mariah's "Without you" popular on talent searches|publisher=The Mariah Carey Archives|access-date=9 April 2012}}</ref> "Without You" was later included on some non-US pressings of her compilation albums ''[[Number 1's (Mariah Carey album)|#1's]]'' (1998) and ''[[Number 1 to Infinity|#1 to Infinity]]'' (2015), and her 2001 compilation, ''[[Greatest Hits (Mariah Carey album)|Greatest Hits]]''. "Without You" was also included on her 2008 compilation ''[[The Ballads (Mariah Carey album)|The Ballads]]''.

"Without You" reached number three on the US [[Billboard Hot 100|''Billboard'' Hot 100]] for six weeks. "Without You" remains Carey's biggest hit across Europe. In the United Kingdom, where Carey had yet to score a number one hit, "Without You" made its UK chart debut at number one where it remained for four weeks in total, and later ended as the 7th best-selling single of 1994 in the United Kingdom.<ref>{{cite web|first=Rob|last=Copsey|url=https://www.officialcharts.com/chart-news/official-top-40-best-selling-songs-of-1994__33326/|title=Official Top 40 best-selling songs of 1994|publisher=Official Charts Company|date=11 June 2021|access-date=13 June 2021|archive-date=6 November 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211106205705/https://www.officialcharts.com/chart-news/official-top-40-best-selling-songs-of-1994__33326/|url-status=live}}</ref> It topped the [[European Hot 100 Singles]] chart for two weeks and reached number one for ten weeks in Switzerland; eight weeks in Austria and Sweden; seven weeks in Belgium; five weeks in Ireland and the Netherlands; four weeks in Germany and Iceland; and two weeks in Scotland.

